Installing and setting up QGIS

This section covers the software and base map required for the workflow. Complete these steps before proceeding to the data preparation stage.

1) Install QGIS

Download QGIS Long-Term Release (LTR) from the QGIS website. The LTR version is recommended because it provides a stable environment without requiring regular updates. 

2) Set up a basemap 

We will use OpenStreetMap (QuickOSM) as the base map for locating and displaying geographic features. 

In QGIS, open Plugins → Manage and Install Plugins.

Search for QuickOSM, select the plugin, and click Install Plugin.

![qgis-basics-historians/images/quickosm]

Once installed, QuickOSM will be available under the Plugins menu. This basemap provides contemporary geographic reference data: roads, settlements, rivers, borders, and other features. 

3) Create a QGIS project

From the Project menu, create a new QGIS project and save it in a dedicated folder.


